; d_king: the final boss, the Bulldog King. Fast and relentless: his motif pumps in the bass
; the whole time, the band hammers double-time, and the cat's motif fights its way up over
; him in the middle. No vibrato anywhere: every note hits.
; Key: D minor, leaning phrygian (Eb) and on the tritone D-G# (the King's motif's own).
;   A  bars 1-8    D pedal: the King's motif as the bass riff (pumping), the same motif on
;                  the lead, sequenced up a fourth and a fifth, then tumbling down
;   B  bars 9-16   Dm Bb C D (2 bars each): the bass pumps the roots; the cat's motif on the
;                  lead, its leap growing (a fifth, a sixth, a sixth), landing on a held D6;
;                  the King's motif growls under it, low, every other phrase
;   C  bars 17-20  the breakdown: a low D pumping, then G# (the tritone) and A; the King's
;                  motif slowed to half speed on the lead; half-time stomps, a roll back in
; Tempo: an 8th is 10 ticks (quarter = 180 bpm), 4/4, a bar of 80 ticks (1.3 s).
; Repeats: 20 bars, 1600 ticks (26.7 s).
; Size: 389 bytes.
;
; Where the motifs are:
;   the King's motif (D G G# G Bb | C D, the cat's turned upside down): the bass riff all
;     through A, every 2 bars; the lead in A bars 1-2, on G in 3-4 (G C C# C Eb | F G) and on
;     A in 5-6; low on voice 1 in B bars 9-10 and 13-14; the lead at half speed in C
;   the Catwiz motif in D minor (D A G# A F | E D): the lead in B bars 9-10, then in its
;     rhythm on Bb (D Bb A Bb F) and C (E C B C G), and up to D6 (A D C# D E | D6)
;   the twitch G# A in the cat's motif is the King's tritone G#: the same note, two meanings
;
; Left (chip 1): bass, tolling pad or the King's low growl, hats. Right (chip 2): the lead,
;   kick and snare. Voice 5 is left free (the enemies' effects have it to themselves).
; voice 0  bass: the left chip's hardware envelope, a falling saw every 5 ticks (h8:332),
;          pumping each held note in 16ths at full level (louder than the battle song, as
;          a_king)
; voice 1  A: a tolling tritone, D and G# in quarters; B: the King's motif low; C: silent
; voice 2  hats, 16ths (noise; lent to the hero's effects)
; voice 3  the lead, loud (v14): staccato in A, longer in B, half speed in C
; voice 4  kick and snare, double time: kick kick snare kick, a fill every 2nd bar; C half
;          time, then the right chip's envelope as a roll
(pattern riff "h8:332 l10 d2 l30 g1 l10 g#1 g1 l20 a#1 l10 c2 l30 d2 l40 d1")
(pattern roots "h8:332 l40 d2 - - - a#1 - - - c2 - - - d2 - - -")
(pattern brk "h8:332 l40 d1 - - - g#1 - a1 -")
(pattern la
    "v14 k3 l10 d5 l30 g4 l10 g#4 g4 l20 a#4 l10 c5 l30 d5 l40 r l10 g5 l30 c5 l10 c#5 c5 l20 d#5 l10 f5 l30 g5 l40 r l10 a5 l30 d5 l10 d#5 d5 l20 f5 l10 g5 l30 a5 l40 r l10 d6 c6 a#5 a5 g#5 a5 g5 f5 l40 d5 l10 a4 a#4 c5 c#5")
(pattern lb
    "k3 l10 d5 l30 a5 l10 g#5 a5 l20 f5 l10 e5 l30 d5 l40 r l10 d5 l30 a#5 l10 a5 a#5 l20 f5 l10 g5 l30 a5 l40 r l10 e5 l30 c6 l10 b5 c6 l20 g5 l10 a5 l30 b5 l40 r l10 a5 l30 d6 l10 c#6 d6 l20 e6 k6 l40 d6 -")
(pattern lc "k4 l20 d5 l60 g4 l20 g#4 g4 l40 a#4 l20 c5 l60 d5 l20 a4 a#4 b4 c#5")
(pattern toll "l40 v11 k4 d4 d4 d4 d4 g#3 g#3 g#3 g#3")
